  "question": {
    "text": "$\\int_{0}^{100} e^{x-[x]} d x$ is equal to",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "p98U4",
      "text": "$\\frac{e^{100}-1}{100}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "DSzCG",
      "text": "$\\frac{e^{100}-1}{e-1}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "EARgo",
      "text": "$100(e-1)$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "YXKQy",
      "text": "$\\frac{e-1}{100}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $I=\\int_{0}^{100} e^{x-[x]} d x$\r\n$=100 \\int_{0}^{1} e^{x-[x]} d x$\r\n$[\\because x-[x]$ is a periodic function of period 1 and $\\int_{0}^{mT} f(x) d x=m \\int_{0}^{T} f(x) d x,$ where $T$ is period of $f(x)]$ $=100 \\int_{0}^{1} e^{x} d x[\\because x-[x]=x$ for $0    < x < 1]$\r\n$=100\\left[e^{x}\\right]_{0}^{1}$\r\n$=100\\left[e^{1}-e^{0}\\right]$\r\n$=100(e-1)$",
    "image": null
  },
